Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 07:18:38 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 13/19] HIP GCN: GEMM flash attention through rocBLAS for head
 size >= 512

Attention as rocBLAS GEMMs on GCN, which has no MFMA/WMMA (Kmic-68's cuBLAS
attention, via qr0n/p100-llama-cpp): by default for head size >= 512 (Gemma 4's global layers), fp32, tuned solutions,
chunks sized by bytes so it fits beside a drafter. Lazy rescale: each row's reference max moves only when
a chunk passes it by more than 8, and the PV GEMM accumulates into O. Test errors 1.73e-4 / 0.84e-4 (as
precise as the tile kernel). MI25, 2048 tokens at 16k: 204 -> 151 ms; Gemma 4 12B 20k read 417 -> 441 t/s.
GGML_CUDA_FA_GEMM=0 turns it off, =1 sends every supported shape; GGML_CUDA_FA_GEMM_PREC=16 for fp16;
GGML_CUDA_FA_GEMM_LAZY=0 for the per-chunk rescale.

